    },
    {
      "image": "videos/02-model-collapse/2.jpg",
      "seconds": 20.58,
      "text": "These systems learned to write by reading the open internet. But the internet is now filling with text written by machines. So the next generation trains on the last one's output. Researchers at Oxford and Cambridge tested this directly. Train a model on its own generations, again and again, and it degrades. The rare, the strange, the specific all vanish first. They called it model collapse.",
      "delivery": {
        "rate": 12,
        "pitch": 0
      },
      "clips": [
        {
          "src": "videos/02-model-collapse/v2-1.mp3",
