      ]
    },
    {
      "image": "videos/02-model-collapse/3.jpg",
      "seconds": 19.93,
      "text": "It's a photocopy of a photocopy. The first copy looks fine. By the hundredth, the face is gone. And the first thing lost is never the average. It's the edge. The outlier. The minority view. Which is why some labs now treat text written before 2022 the way salvage yards treat steel forged before the first atomic tests. Uncontaminated. And finite.",
